TITLE:: SynthDesk
SUMMARY:: A user interface for adding effects to hardware synthesizers
CATEGORIES:: External Control
RELATED:: Classes/Config, Classes/FxBankSynth, Classes/FxBankChorus, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SCViewHolder

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SynthDesk:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that routes hardware synths defined in LINK::Classes/Config:: into SuperCollider so effects can be added to them. It does not create a window. LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: embeds an instance as a page in its stack; the header Synths button (between Record and the MIDI indicator) shows that page. To show the desk on its own, place it in a LINK::Classes/Window:: layout.

Constructing TELETYPE::SynthDesk:: calls LINK::Classes/Setup#*server:: so the LINK::Classes/Server:: is started.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::SynthDesk::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SynthDesk:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: init, prBuildDesk, prSetupHardwareSynth

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Embed in a window
Window("Synths").layout_(VLayout(SynthDesk())).front;

// Or open SequencerGui and click Synths in the header
::
